<div class="ltx_page_main">
<div class="ltx_page_content">
<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line">
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_document">Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces</h1>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Vassil Kanev
</span></span></div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">Graber, Harris and Starr proved, when <math id="abstract1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2d</annotation></semantics></math>, the irreducibility of
the Hurwitz space
<math id="abstract1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{0}_{d,n}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{0}_{d,n}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> which
parametrizes degree <math id="abstract1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> coverings of a smooth, projective curve <math id="abstract1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>
of genus <math id="abstract1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, simply branched in <math id="abstract1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> points, with full monodromy
group <math id="abstract1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. We sharpen this result and prove
that <math id="abstract1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{0}_{d,n}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{0}_{d,n}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> is irreducible if <math id="abstract1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq\max\{2,2d-4\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq\max\{2,2d-4\}</annotation></semantics></math> and
in the case of elliptic <math id="abstract1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="abstract1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq\max\{2,2d-6\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq\max\{2,2d-6\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We extend the result to coverings simply branched in all but one point of the discriminant.
Fixing the
ramification multiplicities over the special point we prove that
the corresponding
Hurwitz space is irreducible if the number of simply branched points
is <math id="abstract1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 2d-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 2d-2</annotation></semantics></math>. We study also simply branched coverings with monodromy
group <math id="abstract1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\neq S_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\neq S_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and when <math id="abstract1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is large enough determine the corresponding connected components of <math id="abstract1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{d,n}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{d,n}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>. Our results are based on explicit calculation of the
braid moves associated with the standard generators of the <math id="abstract1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-strand
braid group of <math id="abstract1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
  
</div><span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup>
      
    Preprint N. 241, Dipartimento di Matematica, Università di Palermo.
<br class="ltx_break">  2000 <em id="footnote1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Mathematics Subject Classification.</em>  Primary: 
14H10;  Secondary:  14H30,  20F36.
</span></span></span>
<section id="Sx1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Introduction</h2>

<div id="Sx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Sx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> be a smooth, connected, projective complex curve of genus
<math id="Sx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Sx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{d,n}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{d,n}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> be the Hurwitz space
which parametrizes degree <math id="Sx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> coverings of <math id="Sx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> simply branched in <math id="Sx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> points. A classical result of Hurwitz <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu</a>]</cite> states that
<math id="Sx1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{d,n}(\mathbb{P}^{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{d,n}(\mathbb{P}^{1})</annotation></semantics></math> is irreducible. More generally one
can consider coverings of <math id="Sx1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> which are simply branched in
all but one point of the discriminant. Fixing the ramification multiplicities
over the special point one obtains a corresponding Hurwitz space which turns
out to be irreducible as well (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Na</a>]</cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kl</a>]</cite>,
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mo</a>]</cite>).</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Coverings of curves of positive genus were studied by Graber, Harris
and Starr in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx6" title="" class="ltx_ref">GHS</a>]</cite>. They considered the Hurwitz space
<math id="Sx1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{0}_{d,n}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{0}_{d,n}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> which parametrizes coverings with full
monodromy group <math id="Sx1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and proved it is irreducible if <math id="Sx1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2d</annotation></semantics></math>.
Another result of this type was obtained by F. Vetro <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ve</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In the present paper we sharpen the result of Graber, Harris and Starr
and prove that <math id="Sx1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{0}_{d,n}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{0}_{d,n}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> is irreducible if <math id="Sx1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2d-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2d-2</annotation></semantics></math> (cf. Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm10" title="Theorem 3.10. ‣ 3 The case 
        
          
            ≥
            n
            
              -
              
                ⁢
                2
                d
              
              2 ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.10</span></a>). Our approach allows to extend the
result to coverings which are simply branched in all but one point
of the discriminant. Fixing the branching data of the special point,
i.e. a partition
<math id="Sx1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{e}=\{e_{1},e_{2},\ldots,e_{q}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{e}=\{e_{1},e_{2},\ldots,e_{q}\}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="Sx1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1}\geq e_{2}\geq\ldots\geq e_{q}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1}\geq e_{2}\geq\ldots\geq e_{q}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1}+\cdots+e_{q}=d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1}+\cdots+e_{q}=d</annotation></semantics></math> one obtains a Hurwitz space
<math id="Sx1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{0}_{d,n,\underline{e}}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{0}_{d,n,\underline{e}}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> parametrizing coverings with
full monodromy group, simply branched in <math id="Sx1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> points and ramified with
multiplicities <math id="Sx1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1},\ldots,e_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1},\ldots,e_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> over one additional point. We prove
<math id="Sx1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{0}_{d,n,\underline{e}}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{0}_{d,n,\underline{e}}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> is irreducible if <math id="Sx1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2d-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2d-2</annotation></semantics></math>
(cf. Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm11" title="Theorem 3.11. ‣ 3 The case 
        
          
            ≥
            n
            
              -
              
                ⁢
                2
                d
              
              2 ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.11</span></a>). Coverings with <math id="Sx1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n&lt;2d-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n&lt;2d-2</annotation></semantics></math> are more difficult
to deal with. We prove the irreducibility of <math id="Sx1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{0}_{d,n}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{0}_{d,n}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>
when <math id="Sx1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=2d-4,\;d\geq 3,\;g(Y)\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=2d-4,\;d\geq 3,\;g(Y)\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> (cf. Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmthm5" title="Theorem 4.5. ‣ 4 The case 
        
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              
                =
                n
                
                  -
                  
                    ⁢
                    2
                    d
                  
                  4
                
              
              ,
              
                ≥
                g
                1 ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>)
and the irreducibility of <math id="Sx1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{0}_{d,n}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{0}_{d,n}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="Sx1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=2d-6,\;d\geq 4,\;g(Y)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=2d-6,\;d\geq 4,\;g(Y)=1</annotation></semantics></math> (cf. Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmthm4" title="Theorem 5.4. ‣ 5 The case 
        
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              
                =
                n
                
                  -
                  
                    ⁢
                    2
                    d
                  
                  6
                
              
              ,
              
                =
                g
                1 ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>). The case of simply branched coverings
with monodromy groups <math id="Sx1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\neq S_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\neq S_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> can be reduced via étale
coverings to the case of coverings with full monodromy group. In
Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm14" title="Theorem 3.14. ‣ 3 The case 
        
          
            ≥
            n
            
              -
              
                ⁢
                2
                d
              
              2 ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.14</span></a> and Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmthm5" title="Theorem 5.5. ‣ 5 The case 
        
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              
                =
                n
                
                  -
                  
                    ⁢
                    2
                    d
                  
                  6
                
              
              ,
              
                =
                g
                1 ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.5</span></a> we prove that connected
components of <math id="Sx1.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{d,n}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{d,n}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> not contained in
<math id="Sx1.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{0}_{d,n}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{0}_{d,n}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> may exist only if <math id="Sx1.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is not prime and in
this case if <math id="Sx1.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently large such connected components
correspond bijectively to the equivalence classes of étale
coverings <math id="Sx1.p3.m21" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[\tilde{Y}\to Y]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\tilde{Y}\to Y]</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="Sx1.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Sx1.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{2}|d,\;d_{2}\neq 1,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{2}|d,\;d_{2}\neq 1,d</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In proving these results we follow the standard approach for
determining the connected components of <math id="Sx1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{d,n}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{d,n}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Associating to every equivalence class of coverings <math id="Sx1.p4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[X\to Y]\in\mathcal{H}_{d,n}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[X\to Y]\in\mathcal{H}_{d,n}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> its
discriminant locus yields an étale mapping
<math id="Sx1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{d,n}(Y)\to Y^{(n)}-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{d,n}(Y)\to Y^{(n)}-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Fixing a <math id="Sx1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\in Y^{(n)}-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\in Y^{(n)}-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> the fiber over <math id="Sx1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is identified via Riemann’s
existence theorem to the equivalence classes modulo inner
automorphisms of ordered <math id="Sx1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n+2g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n+2g)</annotation></semantics></math>-tuples
<math id="Sx1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying
<math id="Sx1.p4.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="t_{1}\cdots t_{n}=[\lambda_{1},\mu_{1}]\cdots[\lambda_{g},\mu_{g}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1}\cdots t_{n}=[\lambda_{1},\mu_{1}]\cdots[\lambda_{g},\mu_{g}]</annotation></semantics></math>
– we call such <math id="Sx1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n+2g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n+2g)</annotation></semantics></math>-tuples <em id="Sx1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Hurwitz systems</em> – where
<math id="Sx1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i},\lambda_{k},\mu_{k}\in S_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i},\lambda_{k},\mu_{k}\in S_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,   <math id="Sx1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are
transpositions, and <math id="Sx1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i},\lambda_{k},\mu_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i},\lambda_{k},\mu_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Sx1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n,\;1\leq k\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n,\;1\leq k\leq g</annotation></semantics></math>
generate a transitive subgroup of <math id="Sx1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. The problem is thus reduced
to finding the orbits of the action of the <math id="Sx1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-strand braid group of
<math id="Sx1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>, namely <math id="Sx1.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}(Y^{(n)}-\Delta,D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}(Y^{(n)}-\Delta,D)</annotation></semantics></math>, on the set of equivalence
classes of Hurwitz systems. In fact it is more natural and it suffices
to study the action of the braid group of the open Riemann surface
<math id="Sx1.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y-\{b_{0}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y-\{b_{0}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Sx1.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is a fixed point. Birman found in
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bi</a>]</cite> a natural system of generators of these braid groups. Our
results are based on Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm8" title="Theorem 1.8. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.8</span></a> where we calculate explicitly
how these generators act on Hurwitz systems.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We follow the
key idea of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx6" title="" class="ltx_ref">GHS</a>]</cite> which consists in applying a sequence of braid
moves to a given Hurwitz system
<math id="Sx1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g})</annotation></semantics></math> in order to replace
it
by a new one
<math id="Sx1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{t}_{1},\ldots,\tilde{t}_{n};\tilde{\lambda}_{1},\tilde{\mu}_{1},\ldots,\tilde{\lambda}_{g},\tilde{\mu}_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{t}_{1},\ldots,\tilde{t}_{n};\tilde{\lambda}_{1},\tilde{\mu}_{1},\ldots,\tilde{\lambda}_{g},\tilde{\mu}_{g})</annotation></semantics></math> in which as many as possible of the
elements <math id="Sx1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\lambda}_{k},\tilde{\mu}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\lambda}_{k},\tilde{\mu}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> equal 1 and then
reduce the sequence <math id="Sx1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{t}_{1}\ldots,\tilde{t}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{t}_{1}\ldots,\tilde{t}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> to a
normal form using only elementary transformations of the Artin’s braid
group. An important tool in our arguments is Main
Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmthm1" title="Main Lemma 2.1. ‣ 2 The main lemma ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> which states that if in a Hurwitz system
<math id="Sx1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g})</annotation></semantics></math> one has
<math id="Sx1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}t_{i+1}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}t_{i+1}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, then replacing the pair <math id="Sx1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{i},t_{i+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{i},t_{i+1})</annotation></semantics></math> by a pair
<math id="Sx1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(h^{-1}t_{i}h,h^{-1}t_{i+1}h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(h^{-1}t_{i}h,h^{-1}t_{i+1}h)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Sx1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to the subgroup generated by
<math id="Sx1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{j},\lambda_{k},\mu_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{j},\lambda_{k},\mu_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Sx1.p5.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1\leq j\leq n,\,j\neq i,i+1,\,1\leq k\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq j\leq n,\,j\neq i,i+1,\,1\leq k\leq g</annotation></semantics></math>,
one obtains a braid-equivalent Hurwitz system, i.e. can be
obtained from the initial one by a finite sequence of braid moves. This
is a generalization of Lemma 2.2 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx6" title="" class="ltx_ref">GHS</a>]</cite> proved there using the Kontsevich
moduli space of stable maps. The proof of our Main
Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmthm1" title="Main Lemma 2.1. ‣ 2 The main lemma ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> is more elementary and uses only the explicit formulas
for the braid moves of Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm8" title="Theorem 1.8. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.8</span></a>. We think
Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm8" title="Theorem 1.8. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.8</span></a> and Main Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmthm1" title="Main Lemma 2.1. ‣ 2 The main lemma ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> are results of independent
interest, since both are valid for Hurwitz systems with values in an
arbitrary (possibly infinite) group <math id="Sx1.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>. We profitted a lot from the
paper of Mochizuki <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mo</a>]</cite> which was the starting point for us in
studying the problem of the irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmnotationx1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_notation">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmnotationx1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Notation and conventions</span></span><span id="Thmnotationx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmnotationx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmnotationx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We assume that the base field <math id="Thmnotationx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Throughout the paper <math id="Thmnotationx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:X\to Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:X\to Y</annotation></semantics></math> denotes a covering, i.e. a finite holomorphic mapping, of smooth projective curves.
We do not assume that <math id="Thmnotationx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is connected, while <math id="Thmnotationx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> is always assumed connected.
Two coverings <math id="Thmnotationx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}:X_{1}\to Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}:X_{1}\to Y</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmnotationx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{2}:X_{2}\to Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{2}:X_{2}\to Y</annotation></semantics></math> are called equivalent if there is an isomorphism <math id="Thmnotationx1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:X_{1}\to X_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:X_{1}\to X_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmnotationx1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}=\pi_{2}\circ f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}=\pi_{2}\circ f</annotation></semantics></math>. A covering <math id="Thmnotationx1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:X\to Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:X\to Y</annotation></semantics></math> of degree
<math id="Thmnotationx1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is called simple if both <math id="Thmnotationx1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmnotationx1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> are irreducible
and for each <math id="Thmnotationx1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in Y</annotation></semantics></math> one has <math id="Thmnotationx1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d-1\leq\#\;\pi^{-1}(y)\leq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d-1\leq\#\;\pi^{-1}(y)\leq d</annotation></semantics></math>. We use mainly right actions and write <math id="Thmnotationx1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>g</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{g}</annotation></semantics></math> for
<math id="Thmnotationx1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmnotationx1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in G</annotation></semantics></math>, where the group <math id="Thmnotationx1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> acts on the set <math id="Thmnotationx1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> on the right. In particular if <math id="Thmnotationx1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=G</annotation></semantics></math> we let <math id="Thmnotationx1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{g}=g^{-1}xg" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>g</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{g}=g^{-1}xg</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmcontentsx1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_contents">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmcontentsx1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Contents</span></span><span id="Thmcontentsx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmcontentsx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmcontentsx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">1. Braid moves, 
2. The main lemma, 
3. The case <math id="Thmcontentsx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2d-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2d-2</annotation></semantics></math>,
4. The case <math id="Thmcontentsx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=2d-4,\quad g\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=2d-4,\quad g\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, 
5. The case <math id="Thmcontentsx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=2d-6,\&gt;g=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.387em">,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=2d-6,\&gt;g=1</annotation></semantics></math>. </p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Braid moves</h2>

<div id="S1.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_block">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmthm1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.1</span></span><span id="S1.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The equivalence classes of (possibly nonconnected) coverings of degree <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> of
a smooth,
projective, irreducible curve <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> branched in <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> points are
parametrized by a smooth scheme <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> which is an
étale cover of <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{(n)}-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{(n)}-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Here <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is the codimension
one subscheme consisting of nonsimple divisors of degree <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. The
covering mapping associates to <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[X\to Y]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[X\to Y]</annotation></semantics></math> its branch locus <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. Let
<math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}\in Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}\in Y</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote by <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}(b_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}(b_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>
the open subset of <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> consisting of coverings which are
unramified at
<math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly we consider equivalence classes of pairs <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[\pi:X\to Y,\phi]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\pi:X\to Y,\phi]</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[X\to Y]\in\mathcal{U}(b_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[X\to Y]\in\mathcal{U}(b_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:\pi^{-1}(b_{0})\to\{1,\ldots,d\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:\pi^{-1}(b_{0})\to\{1,\ldots,d\}</annotation></semantics></math> is a bijection. We denote by
<math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y,b_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y,b_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> the corresponding étale cover of
<math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}(b_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}(b_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\in Y^{(n)}-\Delta,\;b_{0}\notin D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∉</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\in Y^{(n)}-\Delta,\;b_{0}\notin D</annotation></semantics></math>. Riemann’s existence theorem (see e.g. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fu</a>]</cite> p.544)
establishes the following natural one-to-one correspondences</p>
<ol id="S1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">A.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y,b_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y,b_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> between:</p>
<ol id="S1.I1.i1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S1.I1.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the fiber of <math id="S1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y,b_{0})\to(Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y,b_{0})\to(Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the set of homomorphisms <math id="S1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m:\pi_{1}(Y-D,b_{0})\to S_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m:\pi_{1}(Y-D,b_{0})\to S_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>
which satisfy the condition that <math id="S1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\gamma)\neq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\gamma)\neq 1</annotation></semantics></math> for each small loop which
circles a point of <math id="S1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">B.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> between:</p>
<ol id="S1.I1.i2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S1.I1.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the fiber of
<math id="S1.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y)\to Y^{(n)}-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y)\to Y^{(n)}-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S1.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the set of equivalence classes modulo inner
automorphisms of homomorphisms
<math id="S1.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m:\pi_{1}(Y-D,b_{0})\to S_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m:\pi_{1}(Y-D,b_{0})\to S_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the condition of A(ii), here <math id="S1.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\sim m^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\sim m^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>
if there exists an <math id="S1.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in S_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in S_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="S1.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\prime}=s^{-1}ms" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\prime}=s^{-1}ms</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We fix our preferences in this paper as follows. We consider the
product in a fundamental group induced by product of arcs defined as</p>
<table id="S1.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1}*\gamma_{2}=\begin{cases}\gamma_{1}(2t)&amp;\text{for $0\leq t\leq 1/2$},\\
\gamma_{2}(2t-1)&amp;\text{for $1/2\leq t\leq 1$}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1}*\gamma_{2}=\begin{cases}\gamma_{1}(2t)&amp;\text{for $0\leq t\leq 1/2$},\\
\gamma_{2}(2t-1)&amp;\text{for $1/2\leq t\leq 1$}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We consider right action of <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,\ldots,d\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,\ldots,d\}</annotation></semantics></math>, so a
permutation <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in S_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in S_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> transforms <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i^{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>i</mi><mi>σ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> and for instance
<math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(123)=(12)(13)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>123</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>12</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>13</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(123)=(12)(13)</annotation></semantics></math>. Explicitly the correspondence in (A) is defined in
the following way. Given a pair <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:X\to Y,\quad\phi:\pi^{-1}(b_{0})\to\{1,\ldots,d\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:X\to Y,\quad\phi:\pi^{-1}(b_{0})\to\{1,\ldots,d\}</annotation></semantics></math> let us number the elements of the fiber <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{-1}(b_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{-1}(b_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> using
<math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, thus <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{-1}(b_{0})=\{x_{1},\ldots,x_{d}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{-1}(b_{0})=\{x_{1},\ldots,x_{d}\}</annotation></semantics></math> where
<math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}=\phi^{-1}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}=\phi^{-1}(i)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then given a homotopy class of loops <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\gamma]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\gamma]</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(0)=\gamma(1)=b_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(0)=\gamma(1)=b_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> the permutation <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=m(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=m(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>
acts as follows. If lifting <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> one starts from <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and ends
at <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, then one lets <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i^{\sigma}=j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mi>σ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{\sigma}=j</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in S_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in S_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Renumbering
the points of the fiber <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{-1}(b_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{-1}(b_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> by a bijective map <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi:\pi^{-1}(b_{0})\to\{1,\ldots,d\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi:\pi^{-1}(b_{0})\to\{1,\ldots,d\}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(x)=\phi(x)^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(x)=\phi(x)^{s}</annotation></semantics></math>
results in replacing the monodromy homomorphism <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{-1}ms" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{-1}ms</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence the one-to-one correspondence in (B) is obtained from that of (A)
applying the forgetful mapping <math id="S1.Thmthm1.p1.m44" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[X\to Y,\;\phi]\mapsto[X\to Y]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[X\to Y,\;\phi]\mapsto[X\to Y]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_block">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmthm2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.2</span></span><span id="S1.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose that <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(Y)\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(Y)\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us fix the orientation of the real 2-manifold
<math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> considered as a complex manifold. Let <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\{b_{1},\ldots,b_{n}\}\subset Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\{b_{1},\ldots,b_{n}\}\subset Y</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}\notin D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∉</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}\notin D</annotation></semantics></math>.
We describe a standard way of choosing generators of <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}(Y-D,b_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}(Y-D,b_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Cutting <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> along <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2g</annotation></semantics></math> simple closed arcs which begin at <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and do
not contain any of <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i},\;i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i},\;i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> one obtains a standard
<math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4g</annotation></semantics></math>-polygon with sides
<math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1},\beta_{1},\alpha_{1}^{-1},\beta_{1}^{-1},\ldots,\alpha_{g},\beta_{g},\alpha_{g}^{-1},\beta_{g}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1},\beta_{1},\alpha_{1}^{-1},\beta_{1}^{-1},\ldots,\alpha_{g},\beta_{g},\alpha_{g}^{-1},\beta_{g}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> which circle the polygon
in counterclockwise direction. We consider a simple closed arc <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>
which begins at <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L-b_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L-b_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in the interior
of the 4g-polygon and passes consecutively in counterclockwise
direction through the points <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{b_{1},\ldots,b_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{b_{1},\ldots,b_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The closed arc <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>
divides the <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4g</annotation></semantics></math> polygon into two regions <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> which stay on the
left respectively on the right side of <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to its counterclockwise
orientation. We choose a simple arc <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> which lies inside the
region <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> and connects <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we choose a second
simple arc <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> inside <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> which connects <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,
has only <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> as point in common with <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and lies on the
left side of <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Continuing in this way we obtain an ordered
<math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-tuple <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\ell_{1}\ldots,\ell_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\ell_{1}\ldots,\ell_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> of simple arcs which do not
meet outside <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> be a closed path which
begins at <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, travels along <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to a point near <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>,
makes a small counterclockwise loop around <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and returns to
<math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> along <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. We obtain a <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n+2g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n+2g)</annotation></semantics></math>-tuple of closed arcs
<math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma_{1},\ldots,\gamma_{n};\alpha_{1},\beta_{1},\ldots,\alpha_{g},\beta_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma_{1},\ldots,\gamma_{n};\alpha_{1},\beta_{1},\ldots,\alpha_{g},\beta_{g})</annotation></semantics></math> which we call a <em id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">standard system of closed
arcs</em>. The corresponding homotopy classes yield a standard
system of generators for <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}(Y-D,b_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}(Y-D,b_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> which satisfy the only
relation</p>
<table id="S1.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\gamma_{1}\gamma_{2}\cdots\gamma_{n}\ \simeq\ [\alpha_{1},\beta_{1}]\cdots[\alpha_{g},\beta_{g}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.778em">≃</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1}\gamma_{2}\cdots\gamma_{n}\ \simeq\ [\alpha_{1},\beta_{1}]\cdots[\alpha_{g},\beta_{g}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.Thmthm2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S1.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 1.2. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> illustrates such a standard system. A reader who
prefers the clockwise orientation of closed arcs and ordering of the
branch points from left to right may look at this and all subsequent
figures from the other side of the sheet.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S1.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="/html/math/0509154/assets/irred1b.png" id="S1.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" width="298" height="278" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>Standard system of closed arcs</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S1.Thmthm2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Given a covering <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:X\to Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:X\to Y</annotation></semantics></math> with discriminant <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> and an
isomorphism <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:\pi^{-1}(b_{0})\to S_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:\pi^{-1}(b_{0})\to S_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> one applies the monodromy
homomorphism <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> and obtains <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}=m(\gamma_{i}),\;\lambda_{k}=m(\alpha_{k}),\;\mu_{k}=\lambda_{g+k}=m(\beta_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}=m(\gamma_{i}),\;\lambda_{k}=m(\alpha_{k}),\;\mu_{k}=\lambda_{g+k}=m(\beta_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdfn1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_dfn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdfn1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdfn1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdfn1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdfn1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An ordered sequence <math id="Thmdfn1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g})</annotation></semantics></math>
of permutations in <math id="Thmdfn1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmdfn1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}\neq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}\neq 1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmdfn1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall i</annotation></semantics></math> and
satisfying the relation</p>
<table id="S1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="t_{1}t_{2}\cdots t_{n}\ =\ [\lambda_{1},\mu_{1}]\cdots[\lambda_{g},\mu_{g}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1}t_{2}\cdots t_{n}\ =\ [\lambda_{1},\mu_{1}]\cdots[\lambda_{g},\mu_{g}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdfn1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is called a <em id="Thmdfn1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Hurwitz system</em>. We let <math id="Thmdfn1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{g+k}=\mu_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{g+k}=\mu_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. We call the
subgroup <math id="Thmdfn1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\subseteq S_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\subseteq S_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>
generated by all <math id="Thmdfn1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i},\lambda_{k},\mu_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i},\lambda_{k},\mu_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> the <em id="Thmdfn1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">monodromy group</em>
of the Hurwitz system.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">By <a href="#S1.Thmthm1" title="1.1. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a> given <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\in Y^{(n)}-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\in Y^{(n)}-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}\notin D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∉</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}\notin D</annotation></semantics></math>, and
fixing the closed arcs <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma_{1},\ldots,\gamma_{n};\alpha_{1},\beta_{1},\ldots,\alpha_{g},\linebreak\beta_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma_{1},\ldots,\gamma_{n};\alpha_{1},\beta_{1},\ldots,\alpha_{g},\linebreak\beta_{g})</annotation></semantics></math> as above, the
fiber of <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y,b_{0})\to(Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y,b_{0})\to(Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> over
<math id="S1.Thmthm2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> may be identified with the set of all Hurwitz systems, while the
fiber of <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y)\to Y^{(n)}-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y)\to Y^{(n)}-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> may be
identified with the set of equivalence classes
<math id="S1.Thmthm2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g}]</annotation></semantics></math>
of Hurwitz systems modulo inner automorphisms of <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, where
<math id="S1.Thmthm2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{1},\ldots,\mu_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{1},\ldots,\mu_{g})</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,\mu^{\prime}_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,\mu^{\prime}_{g})</annotation></semantics></math> if
there exists an <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in S_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in S_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\prime}_{i}=s^{-1}t_{i}s,\;\lambda^{\prime}_{k}=s^{-1}\lambda_{k}s,\;\mu^{\prime}_{k}=s^{-1}\mu_{k}s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\prime}_{i}=s^{-1}t_{i}s,\;\lambda^{\prime}_{k}=s^{-1}\lambda_{k}s,\;\mu^{\prime}_{k}=s^{-1}\mu_{k}s</annotation></semantics></math> for
<math id="S1.Thmthm2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall i,k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall i,k</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">An equivalent way of constructing a standard system of closed arcs is the
following. One chooses first the <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2g</annotation></semantics></math> simple closed arcs
<math id="S1.Thmthm2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1},\beta_{1},\ldots,\alpha_{g},\beta_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1},\beta_{1},\ldots,\alpha_{g},\beta_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then one chooses <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> simple arcs
which start at <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, lie inside the <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4g</annotation></semantics></math>-polygon, do not meet outside <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and have for end points the <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> points of <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>.
One enumerates these arcs
according to the directions of departure in counterclockwise order.
The
obtained <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n+2g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n+2g)</annotation></semantics></math>-tuple <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\ell_{1},\ldots,\ell_{n};\alpha_{1},\beta_{1},\ldots,\alpha_{g},\beta_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\ell_{1},\ldots,\ell_{n};\alpha_{1},\beta_{1},\ldots,\alpha_{g},\beta_{g})</annotation></semantics></math> is called an <em id="S1.Thmthm2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">arc
system</em> (cf. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lo</a>]</cite> p.416).
One considers the induced ordering of the
points of <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. One can take for <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> a star-like region which contains the
union <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}\cup\ldots\cup\ell_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}\cup\ldots\cup\ell_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="S1.Thmthm2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=\partial R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=\partial R</annotation></semantics></math>. In this way one
obtains all ingredients used to construct a standard system of closed arcs
<math id="S1.Thmthm2.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma_{1},\ldots,\gamma_{n};\alpha_{1},\beta_{1},\ldots,\alpha_{g},\beta_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma_{1},\ldots,\gamma_{n};\alpha_{1},\beta_{1},\ldots,\alpha_{g},\beta_{g})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_block">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmthm3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.3</span></span><span id="S1.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The connected components of <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> are in one-to-one
correspondence with the orbits of the full <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-strand braid group
<math id="S1.Thmthm3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}(Y^{(n)}-\Delta,D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}(Y^{(n)}-\Delta,D)</annotation></semantics></math> acting on the fiber of the topological
covering <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y)\to Y^{(n)}-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y)\to Y^{(n)}-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. Similar
statement holds about <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y,b_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y,b_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> where one considers
the braid group <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}((Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta,D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}((Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta,D)</annotation></semantics></math>. The identification
of these fibers with the Hurwitz systems reduces the problem of
determining the connected components of <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y,b_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y,b_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> to calculating the action of the respective braid
groups on Hurwitz systems and then finding the orbits.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i},\alpha_{k},\beta_{k},\;1\leq i\leq n,\&gt;1\leq k\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i},\alpha_{k},\beta_{k},\;1\leq i\leq n,\&gt;1\leq k\leq g</annotation></semantics></math> be a standard system of closed arcs obtained from an arc system <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i},\alpha_{k},\beta_{k},\;1\leq i\leq n,\&gt;1\leq k\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i},\alpha_{k},\beta_{k},\;1\leq i\leq n,\&gt;1\leq k\leq g</annotation></semantics></math>
as in <a href="#S1.Thmthm2" title="1.2. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>. Let <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{u},\;0\leq u\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{u},\;0\leq u\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> be a closed arc in <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{0}=D^{1}=D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{0}=D^{1}=D</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose that starting from the given arc system one can extend the map <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\mapsto D^{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>u</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\mapsto D^{u}</annotation></semantics></math> to a homotopy of arc systems <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}^{u},\alpha_{k}^{u},\beta_{k}^{u},\;1\leq i\leq n,\&gt;1\leq k\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}^{u},\alpha_{k}^{u},\beta_{k}^{u},\;1\leq i\leq n,\&gt;1\leq k\leq g</annotation></semantics></math> based at <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. This yields a corresponding homotopy of closed arcs <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}^{u},\alpha_{k}^{u},\beta_{k}^{u}\;1\leq i\leq n,\&gt;1\leq k\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn> 1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}^{u},\alpha_{k}^{u},\beta_{k}^{u}\;1\leq i\leq n,\&gt;1\leq k\leq g</annotation></semantics></math>
which form a standard system for each <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[X\to Y,\,\phi]\in\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y,b_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[X\to Y,\,\phi]\in\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y,b_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> have discriminant <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> and let
<math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g})</annotation></semantics></math> be the corresponding Hurwitz system. Then the
lifting of the closed arc <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{u},\,0\leq u\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{u},\,0\leq u\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, starting from a <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[X\to Y,\&gt;\phi]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo rspace="0.387em">,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[X\to Y,\&gt;\phi]</annotation></semantics></math>, is defined by
by <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{u}:\pi_{1}(Y-D^{u},b_{0})\to S_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>u</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{u}:\pi_{1}(Y-D^{u},b_{0})\to S_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> where (cf.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fu</a>]</cite> p.545)</p>
<table id="S1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{u}(\gamma_{i}^{u})=t_{i},\quad m^{u}(\alpha_{k}^{u})=\lambda_{k},\quad m^{u}(\beta_{k}^{u})=\mu_{k}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{u}(\gamma_{i}^{u})=t_{i},\quad m^{u}(\alpha_{k}^{u})=\lambda_{k},\quad m^{u}(\beta_{k}^{u})=\mu_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Letting <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{1}_{i}=\gamma^{\prime}_{i},\;\alpha^{1}_{k}=\alpha^{\prime}_{k},\;\beta^{1}_{k}=\beta^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{1}_{i}=\gamma^{\prime}_{i},\;\alpha^{1}_{k}=\alpha^{\prime}_{k},\;\beta^{1}_{k}=\beta^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{1}=m^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{1}=m^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> we obtain the end
point of the lifting of <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{u}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m20" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[X^{\prime}\to Y,\&gt;\phi^{\prime}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo rspace="0.387em">,</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[X^{\prime}\to Y,\&gt;\phi^{\prime}]</annotation></semantics></math> whose
monodromy map <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\prime}:\pi_{1}(Y-D,b_{0})\to S_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\prime}:\pi_{1}(Y-D,b_{0})\to S_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined by</p>
<table id="S1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\prime}(\gamma^{\prime}_{i})=t_{i},\quad m^{\prime}(\alpha^{\prime}_{k})=\lambda_{k},\quad m^{\prime}(\beta^{\prime}_{k})=\mu_{k}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\prime}(\gamma^{\prime}_{i})=t_{i},\quad m^{\prime}(\alpha^{\prime}_{k})=\lambda_{k},\quad m^{\prime}(\beta^{\prime}_{k})=\mu_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Evaluating <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i},\alpha_{k},\beta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i},\alpha_{k},\beta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> we obtain</p>
<table id="S1.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\prime}(\gamma_{i})=t^{\prime}_{i},\quad m^{\prime}(\alpha_{k})=\lambda^{\prime}_{k},\quad m^{\prime}(\beta_{k})=\mu^{\prime}_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\prime}(\gamma_{i})=t^{\prime}_{i},\quad m^{\prime}(\alpha_{k})=\lambda^{\prime}_{k},\quad m^{\prime}(\beta_{k})=\mu^{\prime}_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">So <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,t^{\prime}_{n};\lambda^{\prime}_{1},\mu^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,\lambda^{\prime}_{g},\mu^{\prime}_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,t^{\prime}_{n};\lambda^{\prime}_{1},\mu^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,\lambda^{\prime}_{g},\mu^{\prime}_{g})</annotation></semantics></math>
is the Hurwitz system corresponding to <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m25" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[X^{\prime}\to Y,\&gt;\phi^{\prime}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo rspace="0.387em">,</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[X^{\prime}\to Y,\&gt;\phi^{\prime}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Another
approach is to consider</p>
<table id="S1.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\gamma^{\prime}_{i})=t^{\prime\prime}_{i},\quad m(\alpha^{\prime}_{k})=\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{k},\quad m(\beta^{\prime}_{k})=\mu^{\prime\prime}_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\gamma^{\prime}_{i})=t^{\prime\prime}_{i},\quad m(\alpha^{\prime}_{k})=\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{k},\quad m(\beta^{\prime}_{k})=\mu^{\prime\prime}_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.5" class="ltx_p">The Hurwitz
system <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t^{\prime\prime}_{1},\ldots,t^{\prime\prime}_{n};\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{1},\mu^{\prime\prime}_{1},\ldots,\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{g},\mu^{\prime\prime}_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t^{\prime\prime}_{1},\ldots,t^{\prime\prime}_{n};\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{1},\mu^{\prime\prime}_{1},\ldots,\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{g},\mu^{\prime\prime}_{g})</annotation></semantics></math>
corresponds to a pair <math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m27" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[X^{\prime\prime}\to Y,\&gt;\phi^{\prime\prime}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo rspace="0.387em">,</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[X^{\prime\prime}\to Y,\&gt;\phi^{\prime\prime}]</annotation></semantics></math> whose monodromy map
<math id="S1.Thmthm3.p2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\prime\prime}:\pi_{1}(Y-D,b_{0})\to S_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\prime\prime}:\pi_{1}(Y-D,b_{0})\to S_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</p>
<table id="S1.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\prime\prime}(\gamma_{i})=t^{\prime\prime}_{i},\quad m^{\prime\prime}(\alpha_{k})=\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{k},\quad m^{\prime\prime}(\beta_{k})=\mu^{\prime\prime}_{k}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\prime\prime}(\gamma_{i})=t^{\prime\prime}_{i},\quad m^{\prime\prime}(\alpha_{k})=\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{k},\quad m^{\prime\prime}(\beta_{k})=\mu^{\prime\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmthm4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1.4</span></span><span id="S1.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let us lift the path <math id="S1.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{1-u},\,0\leq u\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{1-u},\,0\leq u\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> starting from <math id="S1.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[X\to Y,\&gt;\phi]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo rspace="0.387em">,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[X\to Y,\&gt;\phi]</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the end point is <math id="S1.Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[X^{\prime\prime}\to Y,\&gt;\phi^{\prime\prime}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo rspace="0.387em">,</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[X^{\prime\prime}\to Y,\&gt;\phi^{\prime\prime}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">In terms of <math id="S1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{\prime}_{i},\alpha^{\prime}_{k},\beta^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{\prime}_{i},\alpha^{\prime}_{k},\beta^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> the monodromy map of
<math id="S1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[X\to Y,\&gt;\phi]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo rspace="0.387em">,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[X\to Y,\&gt;\phi]</annotation></semantics></math> is given by
<math id="S1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\gamma^{\prime}_{i})=t^{\prime\prime}_{i},\;m(\alpha^{\prime}_{k})=\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{k},\;m(\beta^{\prime}_{k})=\mu^{\prime\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\gamma^{\prime}_{i})=t^{\prime\prime}_{i},\;m(\alpha^{\prime}_{k})=\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{k},\;m(\beta^{\prime}_{k})=\mu^{\prime\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us
consider the homotopy of closed paths
<math id="S1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}^{1-u},\alpha_{k}^{1-u},\beta_{k}^{1-u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}^{1-u},\alpha_{k}^{1-u},\beta_{k}^{1-u}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq u\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq u\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and
the path in <math id="S1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y,b_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y,b_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> given by
<math id="S1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{u}:\pi_{1}(Y-D^{1-u},b_{0})\to S_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{u}:\pi_{1}(Y-D^{1-u},b_{0})\to S_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> where
<math id="S1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{u}(\gamma^{1-u}_{i})=t_{i}^{\prime\prime},\,n^{u}(\alpha^{1-u}_{k})=\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{k},\,n^{u}(\beta^{1-u}_{k})=\mu^{\prime\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{u}(\gamma^{1-u}_{i})=t_{i}^{\prime\prime},\,n^{u}(\alpha^{1-u}_{k})=\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{k},\,n^{u}(\beta^{1-u}_{k})=\mu^{\prime\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{0}=m,\;n^{1}=m^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{0}=m,\;n^{1}=m^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (cf.
Eq.(<a href="#S1.E5" title="In 1.3. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>))
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdfn2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_dfn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdfn2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2</span></span><span id="Thmdfn2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdfn2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdfn2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a closed arc <math id="Thmdfn2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{u},\,0\leq u\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{u},\,0\leq u\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> in the configuration space
<math id="Thmdfn2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> the transformation of Hurwitz systems
<math id="Thmdfn2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g})\mapsto(t^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,t^{\prime}_{n};\lambda^{\prime}_{1},\mu^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,\lambda^{\prime}_{g},\linebreak\mu^{\prime}_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g})\mapsto(t^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,t^{\prime}_{n};\lambda^{\prime}_{1},\mu^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,\lambda^{\prime}_{g},\linebreak\mu^{\prime}_{g})</annotation></semantics></math> given
by Eq.(<a href="#S1.E3" title="In 1.3. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) is called a <em id="Thmdfn2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">braid move</em> of the first type.
The transformation <math id="Thmdfn2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\linebreak\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g})\mapsto(t^{\prime\prime}_{1},\ldots,t^{\prime\prime}_{n};\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{1},\mu^{\prime\prime}_{1},\ldots,\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{g},\mu^{\prime\prime}_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\linebreak\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g})\mapsto(t^{\prime\prime}_{1},\ldots,t^{\prime\prime}_{n};\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{1},\mu^{\prime\prime}_{1},\ldots,\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{g},\mu^{\prime\prime}_{g})</annotation></semantics></math> given by Eq.(<a href="#S1.E5" title="In 1.3. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) is called a braid move
of the second type.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The braid moves of the first and of the second
type are inverse to each other according to Lemma <a href="#S1.Thmthm4" title="Lemma 1.4. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.4</span></a>.
It is evident that the braid moves of both types commute with inner
automorphisms of <math id="S1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. So the braid moves are well-defined on
equivalence classes of Hurwitz systems (cf. <a href="#S1.Thmthm2" title="1.2. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_block">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmthm5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.5</span></span><span id="S1.Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There is a convenient system of generators of
<math id="S1.Thmthm5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}((Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta,D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}((Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta,D)</annotation></semantics></math>. We include here some
material borrowed from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bi</a>]</cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sc</a>]</cite> for the sake of
convenience of the reader and since our choices differ slightly from
theirs. Consider the Galois covering
<math id="S1.Thmthm5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p:(Y-b_{0})^{n}\to(Y-b_{0})^{(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p:(Y-b_{0})^{n}\to(Y-b_{0})^{(n)}</annotation></semantics></math> with Galois group <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Restricting to the
complement of <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> one obtains an unramified
Galois covering <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p:(Y-b_{0})^{n}-p^{-1}(\Delta)\to(Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p:(Y-b_{0})^{n}-p^{-1}(\Delta)\to(Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Following the notation of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx4" title="" class="ltx_ref">FN</a>]</cite> if
<math id="S1.Thmthm5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{1}=\{b_{0}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{1}=\{b_{0}\}</annotation></semantics></math> one denotes <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y-b_{0})^{n}-p^{-1}(\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y-b_{0})^{n}-p^{-1}(\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math> by
<math id="S1.Thmthm5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1,n}Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1,n}Y</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\{b_{1},\ldots,b_{n}\},\;\tilde{D}=(b_{1},\ldots,b_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\{b_{1},\ldots,b_{n}\},\;\tilde{D}=(b_{1},\ldots,b_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>.
One has an exact sequence</p>
<table id="S1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\longrightarrow\pi_{1}(F_{1,n}Y,\tilde{D})\longrightarrow\pi_{1}((Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta,D)\longrightarrow S_{n}\longrightarrow 1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\longrightarrow\pi_{1}(F_{1,n}Y,\tilde{D})\longrightarrow\pi_{1}((Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta,D)\longrightarrow S_{n}\longrightarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.Thmthm5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">One determines first a system of generators of the pure braid group
<math id="S1.Thmthm5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}(F_{1,n}Y,\tilde{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}(F_{1,n}Y,\tilde{D})</annotation></semantics></math>
as follows. Consider the closed arcs in <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1,n}Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1,n}Y</annotation></semantics></math> defined by
<math id="S1.Thmthm5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b_{1},\ldots,b_{i-1},r_{ik}(t),b_{i+1},\ldots,b_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b_{1},\ldots,b_{i-1},r_{ik}(t),b_{i+1},\ldots,b_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S1.Thmthm5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b_{1},\ldots,b_{i-1},t_{ik}(t),b_{i+1},\ldots,b_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b_{1},\ldots,b_{i-1},t_{ik}(t),b_{i+1},\ldots,b_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>,
where <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> are the closed simple arcs based at
<math id="S1.Thmthm5.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and pictured on Figure <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 1.5. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> by a continuous
line and by a dotted line respectively.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S1.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="/html/math/0509154/assets/irred2b.png" id="S1.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" width="285" height="288" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>Generators of the pure braid group <math id="S1.F2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}(F_{1,n},\tilde{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}(F_{1,n},\tilde{D})</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S1.Thmthm5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We denote the corresponding homotopy classes by <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{ik},\tau_{ik}\in\pi_{1}(F_{1,n}(Y),\tilde{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{ik},\tau_{ik}\in\pi_{1}(F_{1,n}(Y),\tilde{D})</annotation></semantics></math>. Informally <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math>
corresponds to a loop of the <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th point along <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S1.Thmthm5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to a loop of the <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th point along
<math id="S1.Thmthm5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us denote by <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{ij},\,i&lt;j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{ij},\,i&lt;j</annotation></semantics></math> the element of
<math id="S1.Thmthm5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}(F_{1,n}Y,\tilde{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}(F_{1,n}Y,\tilde{D})</annotation></semantics></math> represented by a closed simple arc in
<math id="S1.Thmthm5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> which leaves fixed <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\neq i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\neq i</annotation></semantics></math> and moves <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>
along the arc pictured on Figure <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 1.5. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. For every <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and
every <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j&gt;i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j&gt;i</annotation></semantics></math> the pictured loop is chosen so as to stay on the left of
all arcs used to construct <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> for
<math id="S1.Thmthm5.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,\ldots,g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,\ldots,g</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmclaimx1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_claim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmclaimx1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim</span></span><span id="Thmclaimx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmclaimx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmclaimx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmclaimx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The pure braid group <math id="Thmclaimx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}(F_{1,n}Y,\tilde{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}(F_{1,n}Y,\tilde{D})</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by
<math id="Thmclaimx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{ik},\tau_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{ik},\tau_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmclaimx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="Thmclaimx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j=1,\ldots,n,\quad i&lt;j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j=1,\ldots,n,\quad i&lt;j</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmclaimx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,\ldots,g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,\ldots,g</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S1.Thmthm5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">This is proved by induction on <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1</annotation></semantics></math> the claim is obvious.
Let <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the fibration <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1,n}Y\to F_{1,n-1}Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1,n}Y\to F_{1,n-1}Y</annotation></semantics></math> defined
by <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y_{1},y_{2},\ldots,y_{n})\to(y_{2},\ldots,y_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y_{1},y_{2},\ldots,y_{n})\to(y_{2},\ldots,y_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>. One has an exact
sequence</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\to\pi_{1}(Y-\{b_{0},b_{2},\ldots,b_{n}\},b_{1})\to\pi_{1}(F_{1,n}Y,(b_{1},\ldots,b_{n}))\to\pi_{1}(F_{1,n-1}Y,(b_{2},\ldots,b_{n}))\to 1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\to\pi_{1}(Y-\{b_{0},b_{2},\ldots,b_{n}\},b_{1})\to\pi_{1}(F_{1,n}Y,(b_{1},\ldots,b_{n}))\to\pi_{1}(F_{1,n-1}Y,(b_{2},\ldots,b_{n}))\to 1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.Thmthm5.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{2}(F_{1,n-1}Y)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{2}(F_{1,n-1}Y)=1</annotation></semantics></math> by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx4" title="" class="ltx_ref">FN</a>]</cite>, Corollary 2.2.
The elements <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{ik},\tau_{ik},A_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{ik},\tau_{ik},A_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> map to
the corresponding elements in <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}(F_{1,n-1}Y,(b_{2},\ldots,b_{n}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}(F_{1,n-1}Y,(b_{2},\ldots,b_{n}))</annotation></semantics></math>.
The group <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}(Y-\{b_{0},b_{2},\ldots,b_{n}\},b_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}(Y-\{b_{0},b_{2},\ldots,b_{n}\},b_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> is freely generated by
elements which map into <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{1,k},\tau_{1,k},A_{1,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{1,k},\tau_{1,k},A_{1,j}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p3.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="j\geq 2,\quad k=1,\ldots,g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq 2,\quad k=1,\ldots,g</annotation></semantics></math>. This shows the claim.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fu</a>]</cite> p.547 and using the notation of <a href="#S1.Thmthm2" title="1.2. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a> let us
denote by <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> the simply connected region of <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> enclosed by the
arcs <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math> and the arc of <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to
<math id="S1.Thmthm5.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. For every <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,n-1</annotation></semantics></math> choose simple arcs
<math id="S1.Thmthm5.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{i}:[0,1]\to Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{i}:[0,1]\to Y</annotation></semantics></math> going from <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S1.Thmthm5.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{\prime}_{i}:[0,1]\to Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{\prime}_{i}:[0,1]\to Y</annotation></semantics></math> going from <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let
<math id="S1.Thmthm5.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}:[0,1]\to Y^{(n)}-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}:[0,1]\to Y^{(n)}-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> be the closed arc</p>
<table id="S1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}(t)\ =\ \{b_{1},\ldots,b_{i-1},\eta_{i}(t),\eta^{\prime}_{i}(t),b_{i+2},\ldots,b_{n}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}(t)\ =\ \{b_{1},\ldots,b_{i-1},\eta_{i}(t),\eta^{\prime}_{i}(t),b_{i+2},\ldots,b_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.Thmthm5.p4.2" class="ltx_p">The homotopy class of <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is denoted by <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. We may
consider <math id="S1.Thmthm5.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}(F_{1,n}(Y),\tilde{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}(F_{1,n}(Y),\tilde{D})</annotation></semantics></math> as embedded in
<math id="S1.Thmthm5.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}((Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta,D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}((Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta,D)</annotation></semantics></math>. The following relations are easy to
verify (cf. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx3" title="" class="ltx_ref">FB</a>]</cite> p.249)</p>
<table id="S1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}&amp;\rho_{i+1,k}\ =\ \sigma_{i}\rho_{ik}\sigma_{i}^{-1},\quad\tau_{i+1,k}\ =\ \sigma_{i}\tau_{ik}\sigma_{i}^{-1}\\
&amp;A_{ij}\ =\ \sigma_{i}^{-1}\cdots\sigma_{j-2}^{-1}\sigma_{j-1}^{2}\sigma_{j-2}\cdots\sigma_{i}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="1.278em" rspace="1.278em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="1.278em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="1.278em">=</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}&amp;\rho_{i+1,k}\ =\ \sigma_{i}\rho_{ik}\sigma_{i}^{-1},\quad\tau_{i+1,k}\ =\ \sigma_{i}\tau_{ik}\sigma_{i}^{-1}\\
&amp;A_{ij}\ =\ \sigma_{i}^{-1}\cdots\sigma_{j-2}^{-1}\sigma_{j-1}^{2}\sigma_{j-2}\cdots\sigma_{i}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_pro">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmthm6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1.6</span></span><span id="S1.Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Birman)<span id="S1.Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S1.Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b\in\mathbb{Z},\quad 1\leq a,b\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b\in\mathbb{Z},\quad 1\leq a,b\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>. The braid group <math id="S1.Thmthm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}((Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta,D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}((Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta,D)</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by
<math id="S1.Thmthm6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j},\rho_{ak},\tau_{bk}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j},\rho_{ak},\tau_{bk}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S1.Thmthm6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq j\leq n-1,\quad 1\leq k\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq j\leq n-1,\quad 1\leq k\leq g</annotation></semantics></math>. The corresponding homotopy classes generate
<math id="S1.Thmthm6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}(Y^{(n)}-\Delta,D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}(Y^{(n)}-\Delta,D)</annotation></semantics></math> as well.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let us consider the exact sequence Eq.(<a href="#S1.E6" title="In 1.5. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>). The braids <math id="S1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> map to the transpositions <math id="S1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j\&gt;j+1),\quad j=1,\ldots,n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.220em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j\&gt;j+1),\quad j=1,\ldots,n-1</annotation></semantics></math> which
generate <math id="S1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. So <math id="S1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j},\rho_{ik},\tau_{ik},A_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j},\rho_{ik},\tau_{ik},A_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="S1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;j</annotation></semantics></math> generate <math id="S1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}((Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta,D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}((Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta,D)</annotation></semantics></math> according to the claim
proved in <a href="#S1.Thmthm5" title="1.5. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.5</span></a>. The relations Eq.(<a href="#S1.E7" title="In 1.5. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) show that the
generators may be reduced as stated in the theorem. The last statement
follows from the surjection <math id="S1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}((Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta,D)\twoheadrightarrow\pi_{1}(Y^{(n)}-\Delta,D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↠</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}((Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta,D)\twoheadrightarrow\pi_{1}(Y^{(n)}-\Delta,D)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We described in <a href="#S1.Thmthm5" title="1.5. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.5</span></a> closed arcs in <math id="S1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>
based at <math id="S1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\{b_{1},\ldots,b_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\{b_{1},\ldots,b_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> whose homotopy classes form a system
of generators <math id="S1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j},\rho_{ik},\tau_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j},\rho_{ik},\tau_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> for
<math id="S1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}((Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta,D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}((Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta,D)</annotation></semantics></math>. Our aim now is for each of these to
construct a homotopy of the standard system of closed
arcs <math id="S1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}^{u},\alpha_{k}^{u},\beta_{k}^{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}^{u},\alpha_{k}^{u},\beta_{k}^{u}</annotation></semantics></math> as in <a href="#S1.Thmthm3" title="1.3. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.3</span></a>.
This will permit us to calculate eventually the corresponding braid
moves of the Hurwitz systems. The calculation of the braid moves
<math id="S1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j},\&gt;j=1,\ldots,n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.387em">,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j},\&gt;j=1,\ldots,n-1</annotation></semantics></math> is due to Hurwitz (cf. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu</a>]</cite> or
e.g. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vo</a>]</cite>, Theorem 10.3). We define closed arcs
<math id="S1.p4.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\delta_{k}:[0,1]\to Y,\&gt;\delta_{k}(0)=\delta_{k}(1)=b_{0},\&gt;k=0,1,\ldots,g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo rspace="0.387em">,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.387em">,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{k}:[0,1]\to Y,\&gt;\delta_{k}(0)=\delta_{k}(1)=b_{0},\&gt;k=0,1,\ldots,g</annotation></semantics></math> as follows. We let <math id="S1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0}(t)=b_{0},\&gt;\forall t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.387em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0}(t)=b_{0},\&gt;\forall t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. We connect the initial vertex of <math id="S1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> with the end
vertex of <math id="S1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> in the <math id="S1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4g</annotation></semantics></math>-polygon of Figure <a href="#S1.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 1.2. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> by a
simple arc which belongs to the region <math id="S1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> on the right of <math id="S1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> (cf.
<a href="#S1.Thmthm2" title="1.2. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>). This yields <math id="S1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. We connect the initial vertex
of <math id="S1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> with the end vertex of <math id="S1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> by a simple
arc which belongs to the region on the right of <math id="S1.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> and on the left of
<math id="S1.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote the corresponding closed arc of <math id="S1.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> by
<math id="S1.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Continuing in this way we obtain
<math id="S1.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{1},\delta_{2},\ldots,\delta_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{1},\delta_{2},\ldots,\delta_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Figure <a href="#S1.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Proof. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).
Clearly <math id="S1.p4.m22" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\delta_{k}\simeq[\alpha_{1},\beta_{1}]\cdots[\alpha_{k},\beta_{k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≃</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{k}\simeq[\alpha_{1},\beta_{1}]\cdots[\alpha_{k},\beta_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S1.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y-D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y-D</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p4.m24" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\delta_{g}\simeq\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>≃</mo><mi>γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{g}\simeq\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> according to Eq.(<a href="#S1.E2" title="In 1.2. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmthm7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1.7</span></span><span id="S1.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> be a compact, closed Riemann surface of genus <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(Y)\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(Y)\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}\in Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}\in Y</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i},\alpha_{k},\beta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i},\alpha_{k},\beta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n,\&gt;1\leq k\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n,\&gt;1\leq k\leq g</annotation></semantics></math> be a standard system of closed arcs as in
<a href="#S1.Thmthm2" title="1.2. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>. Let <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{k},\&gt;k=0,1,\ldots,g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.387em">,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{k},\&gt;k=0,1,\ldots,g</annotation></semantics></math> be the closed arcs
defined above. For each of the closed arcs in <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>
constructed in <a href="#S1.Thmthm5" title="1.5. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.5</span></a> and representing <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j},\rho_{ik},\tau_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j},\rho_{ik},\tau_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> there is a homotopy
<math id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}^{u},\alpha_{k}^{u},\beta_{k}^{u},\&gt;u\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.387em">,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}^{u},\alpha_{k}^{u},\beta_{k}^{u},\&gt;u\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> of the
standard system of closed arcs such that the end system
<math id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{\prime}_{i},\alpha^{\prime}_{k},\beta^{\prime}_{k},\&gt;1\leq i\leq n,\&gt;1\leq k\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{\prime}_{i},\alpha^{\prime}_{k},\beta^{\prime}_{k},\&gt;1\leq i\leq n,\&gt;1\leq k\leq g</annotation></semantics></math> is homotopic to:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm7.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">a. for <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq j\leq n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq j\leq n-1</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma^{\prime}_{i}\simeq\gamma_{i}\quad\text{for $\forall i\neq j,\,j+1$},\quad\alpha^{\prime}_{k}\simeq\alpha_{k},\;\beta^{\prime}_{k}\simeq\beta_{k}\quad\text{for $\forall k$}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma^{\prime}_{i}\simeq\gamma_{i}\quad\text{for $\forall i\neq j,\,j+1$},\quad\alpha^{\prime}_{k}\simeq\alpha_{k},\;\beta^{\prime}_{k}\simeq\beta_{k}\quad\text{for $\forall k$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma^{\prime}_{j}\simeq\gamma_{j+1},\quad\gamma^{\prime}_{j+1}\simeq\gamma^{-1}_{j+1}\gamma_{j}\gamma_{j+1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma^{\prime}_{j}\simeq\gamma_{j+1},\quad\gamma^{\prime}_{j+1}\simeq\gamma^{-1}_{j+1}\gamma_{j}\gamma_{j+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm7.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm7.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">b. for <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n,\&gt;1\leq k\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n,\&gt;1\leq k\leq g</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma^{\prime}_{j}\simeq\gamma_{j}\quad\text{for $\forall j\neq i$},\quad\alpha^{\prime}_{\ell}\simeq\alpha_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell$},\quad\beta^{\prime}_{\ell}\simeq\beta_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell\neq k$}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma^{\prime}_{j}\simeq\gamma_{j}\quad\text{for $\forall j\neq i$},\quad\alpha^{\prime}_{\ell}\simeq\alpha_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell$},\quad\beta^{\prime}_{\ell}\simeq\beta_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell\neq k$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma^{\prime}_{i}\simeq\mu_{ik}\gamma_{i}\mu_{ik}^{-1},\quad\beta^{\prime}_{k}\simeq(\zeta_{ik}\gamma_{i}\zeta_{ik}^{-1})\beta_{k},\quad\text{where}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma^{\prime}_{i}\simeq\mu_{ik}\gamma_{i}\mu_{ik}^{-1},\quad\beta^{\prime}_{k}\simeq(\zeta_{ik}\gamma_{i}\zeta_{ik}^{-1})\beta_{k},\quad\text{where}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{ik}\simeq(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1})^{-1}\delta_{k-1}\alpha_{k}(\delta_{k}^{-1}\delta_{g})(\gamma_{i+1}\cdots\gamma_{n})^{-1},\quad\zeta_{ik}\simeq(\delta_{k}^{-1}\delta_{g})(\gamma_{i+1}\cdots\gamma_{n})^{-1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≃</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≃</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{ik}\simeq(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1})^{-1}\delta_{k-1}\alpha_{k}(\delta_{k}^{-1}\delta_{g})(\gamma_{i+1}\cdots\gamma_{n})^{-1},\quad\zeta_{ik}\simeq(\delta_{k}^{-1}\delta_{g})(\gamma_{i+1}\cdots\gamma_{n})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm7.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm7.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm7.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">c. for <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n,\&gt;1\leq k\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n,\&gt;1\leq k\leq g</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma^{\prime}_{j}\simeq\gamma_{j}\quad\text{for $\forall j\neq i$},\quad\alpha^{\prime}_{\ell}\simeq\alpha_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell\neq k$},\quad\beta^{\prime}_{\ell}\simeq\beta_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell$}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma^{\prime}_{j}\simeq\gamma_{j}\quad\text{for $\forall j\neq i$},\quad\alpha^{\prime}_{\ell}\simeq\alpha_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell\neq k$},\quad\beta^{\prime}_{\ell}\simeq\beta_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma^{\prime}_{i}\simeq\nu_{ik}\gamma_{i}\nu_{ik}^{-1},\quad\alpha^{\prime}_{k}\simeq(\xi_{ik}\gamma_{i}^{-1}\xi_{ik}^{-1})\alpha_{k},\quad\text{where}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma^{\prime}_{i}\simeq\nu_{ik}\gamma_{i}\nu_{ik}^{-1},\quad\alpha^{\prime}_{k}\simeq(\xi_{ik}\gamma_{i}^{-1}\xi_{ik}^{-1})\alpha_{k},\quad\text{where}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\nu_{ik}\simeq\gamma_{i+1}\cdots\gamma_{n}(\delta_{k}^{-1}\delta_{g})^{-1}\beta_{k}\delta_{k-1}^{-1}\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1},\quad\xi_{ik}\simeq\delta_{k-1}^{-1}\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≃</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nu_{ik}\simeq\gamma_{i+1}\cdots\gamma_{n}(\delta_{k}^{-1}\delta_{g})^{-1}\beta_{k}\delta_{k-1}^{-1}\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1},\quad\xi_{ik}\simeq\delta_{k-1}^{-1}\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.Thmthm7.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm7.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each of the inverse closed arcs corresponding to
<math id="S1.Thmthm7.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j}^{-1},\rho_{ik}^{-1},\tau_{ik}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j}^{-1},\rho_{ik}^{-1},\tau_{ik}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> there is a
corresponding homotopy of the standard system
<math id="S1.Thmthm7.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i},\alpha_{k},\beta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i},\alpha_{k},\beta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n,\&gt;1\leq k\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n,\&gt;1\leq k\leq g</annotation></semantics></math>
such that the end system <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{\prime\prime}_{i},\alpha^{\prime\prime}_{k},\beta^{\prime\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{\prime\prime}_{i},\alpha^{\prime\prime}_{k},\beta^{\prime\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S1.Thmthm7.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n,\&gt;1\leq k\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n,\&gt;1\leq k\leq g</annotation></semantics></math>
is homotopic to:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm7.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm7.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm7.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">d. for <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq j\leq n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq j\leq n-1</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma^{\prime\prime}_{i}\simeq\gamma_{i}\quad\text{for $\forall i\neq j,\,j+1$},\quad\alpha^{\prime\prime}_{k}\simeq\alpha_{k},\;\beta^{\prime\prime}_{k}\simeq\beta_{k}\quad\text{for $\forall k$}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma^{\prime\prime}_{i}\simeq\gamma_{i}\quad\text{for $\forall i\neq j,\,j+1$},\quad\alpha^{\prime\prime}_{k}\simeq\alpha_{k},\;\beta^{\prime\prime}_{k}\simeq\beta_{k}\quad\text{for $\forall k$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma^{\prime\prime}_{j}\simeq\gamma_{j}\gamma_{j+1}\gamma^{-1}_{j},\quad\gamma^{\prime\prime}_{j+1}\simeq\gamma_{j}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma^{\prime\prime}_{j}\simeq\gamma_{j}\gamma_{j+1}\gamma^{-1}_{j},\quad\gamma^{\prime\prime}_{j+1}\simeq\gamma_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm7.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm7.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm7.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e. for <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{ik}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{ik}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n,\&gt;1\leq k\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n,\&gt;1\leq k\leq g</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma^{\prime\prime}_{j}\simeq\gamma_{j}\quad\text{for $\forall j\neq i$},\quad\alpha^{\prime\prime}_{\ell}\simeq\alpha_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell$},\quad\beta^{\prime\prime}_{\ell}\simeq\beta_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell\neq k$}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma^{\prime\prime}_{j}\simeq\gamma_{j}\quad\text{for $\forall j\neq i$},\quad\alpha^{\prime\prime}_{\ell}\simeq\alpha_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell$},\quad\beta^{\prime\prime}_{\ell}\simeq\beta_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell\neq k$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma^{\prime\prime}_{i}\simeq\mu_{ik}^{-1}\gamma_{i}\mu_{ik},\quad\beta^{\prime\prime}_{k}\simeq(\tilde{\zeta}_{ik}^{-1}\gamma_{i}^{-1}\tilde{\zeta}_{ik})\beta_{k},\quad\text{where}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma^{\prime\prime}_{i}\simeq\mu_{ik}^{-1}\gamma_{i}\mu_{ik},\quad\beta^{\prime\prime}_{k}\simeq(\tilde{\zeta}_{ik}^{-1}\gamma_{i}^{-1}\tilde{\zeta}_{ik})\beta_{k},\quad\text{where}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{$\mu_{ik}$ is as in (b) and}\quad\tilde{\zeta}_{ik}\simeq(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1})^{-1}\delta_{k-1}\alpha_{k}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> is as in (b) and</mtext></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≃</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{$\mu_{ik}$ is as in (b) and}\quad\tilde{\zeta}_{ik}\simeq(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1})^{-1}\delta_{k-1}\alpha_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm7.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm7.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm7.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">f. for <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{ik}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{ik}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n,\&gt;1\leq k\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n,\&gt;1\leq k\leq g</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma^{\prime\prime}_{j}\simeq\gamma_{j}\quad\text{for $\forall j\neq i$},\quad\alpha^{\prime\prime}_{\ell}\simeq\alpha_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell\neq k$},\quad\beta^{\prime\prime}_{\ell}\simeq\beta_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell$}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma^{\prime\prime}_{j}\simeq\gamma_{j}\quad\text{for $\forall j\neq i$},\quad\alpha^{\prime\prime}_{\ell}\simeq\alpha_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell\neq k$},\quad\beta^{\prime\prime}_{\ell}\simeq\beta_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma^{\prime\prime}_{i}\simeq\nu_{ik}^{-1}\gamma_{i}\nu_{ik},\quad\alpha^{\prime\prime}_{k}\simeq(\tilde{\xi}_{ik}^{-1}\gamma_{i}\tilde{\xi}_{ik})\alpha_{k},\quad\text{where}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma^{\prime\prime}_{i}\simeq\nu_{ik}^{-1}\gamma_{i}\nu_{ik},\quad\alpha^{\prime\prime}_{k}\simeq(\tilde{\xi}_{ik}^{-1}\gamma_{i}\tilde{\xi}_{ik})\alpha_{k},\quad\text{where}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{$\nu_{ik}$ is as in (c) and}\quad\tilde{\xi}_{ik}\simeq(\gamma_{i+1}\cdots\gamma_{n})(\delta_{k}^{-1}\delta_{g})^{-1}\beta_{k}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> is as in (c) and</mtext></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≃</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{$\nu_{ik}$ is as in (c) and}\quad\tilde{\xi}_{ik}\simeq(\gamma_{i+1}\cdots\gamma_{n})(\delta_{k}^{-1}\delta_{g})^{-1}\beta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">(a) Here one moves only <math id="S1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{j+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{j+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Clearly
<math id="S1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{\prime}_{j}\simeq\gamma_{j+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{\prime}_{j}\simeq\gamma_{j+1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{j}\gamma_{j+1}\simeq\gamma^{\prime}_{j}\gamma^{\prime}_{j+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≃</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{j}\gamma_{j+1}\simeq\gamma^{\prime}_{j}\gamma^{\prime}_{j+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{\prime}_{j+1}\simeq\gamma^{-1}_{j+1}\gamma_{j}\gamma_{j+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{\prime}_{j+1}\simeq\gamma^{-1}_{j+1}\gamma_{j}\gamma_{j+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">(b) The effect of the homotopy of
<math id="S1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i},\alpha_{k},\beta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i},\alpha_{k},\beta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> along <math id="S1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> is pictured on
Figure <a href="#S1.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Proof. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S1.F3" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S1.F3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:277.1pt;height:230.3pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-15.4pt,12.8pt) scale(0.9,0.9) ;"><img src="/html/math/0509154/assets/irred3.png" id="S1.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" width="710" height="590" alt="Refer to caption">
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>Homotopy along <math id="S1.F3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">One moves the point <math id="S1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> along the arc <math id="S1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> pictured on
Figure <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 1.5. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and together with it deforms the closed arc
<math id="S1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. At the moment <math id="S1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}^{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}^{u}</annotation></semantics></math> reaches the side
<math id="S1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> one deforms also <math id="S1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> in order that the condition
<math id="S1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}^{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}^{u}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{k}^{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{k}^{u}</annotation></semantics></math> have no points in common except
<math id="S1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> remains valid. None of <math id="S1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S1.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq i</annotation></semantics></math>, or
<math id="S1.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S1.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="S1.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S1.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall\ell\neq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall\ell\neq k</annotation></semantics></math> changes in this homotopy. The effect of cutting <math id="S1.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>
along the closed arcs
<math id="S1.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1},\beta_{1},\ldots,\alpha_{k},\beta^{\prime}_{k},\ldots,\alpha_{g},\beta_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1},\beta_{1},\ldots,\alpha_{k},\beta^{\prime}_{k},\ldots,\alpha_{g},\beta_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> is the same as to cut a region containing <math id="S1.p7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> from
the original <math id="S1.p7.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4g</annotation></semantics></math>-polygon and glue it along the side <math id="S1.p7.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> as
described in Figure <a href="#S1.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Proof. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> (NW) (NW=Northwest). We wish to express <math id="S1.p7.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in
terms of the standard system <math id="S1.p7.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{j},\alpha_{\ell},\beta_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{j},\alpha_{\ell},\beta_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S1.p7.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq j\leq n,1\leq\ell\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq j\leq n,1\leq\ell\leq g</annotation></semantics></math>. The closed arc <math id="S1.p7.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is
pictured in the original <math id="S1.p7.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4g</annotation></semantics></math>-polygon on Figure <a href="#S1.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Proof. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> (NE).
It is clear that <math id="S1.p7.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{\prime}_{i}\simeq\eta_{ik}\gamma_{i}\eta_{ik}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{\prime}_{i}\simeq\eta_{ik}\gamma_{i}\eta_{ik}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>
where <math id="S1.p7.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> is the closed arc pictured on
Figure <a href="#S1.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Proof. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> (SW). That <math id="S1.p7.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> is homotopic to
<math id="S1.p7.m29" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1})^{-1}(\delta_{k-1}\alpha_{k})\delta_{k}^{-1}(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1})^{-1}(\delta_{k-1}\alpha_{k})\delta_{k}^{-1}(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1})</annotation></semantics></math> is evident from Figure <a href="#S1.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Proof. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> (SE).
Furthermore <math id="S1.p7.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{ik}\gamma_{i}\eta_{ik}^{-1}\simeq(\eta_{ik}\gamma_{i})\gamma_{i}(\eta_{ik}\gamma_{i})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≃</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{ik}\gamma_{i}\eta_{ik}^{-1}\simeq(\eta_{ik}\gamma_{i})\gamma_{i}(\eta_{ik}\gamma_{i})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the
relation <math id="S1.p7.m31" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{n}\simeq\delta_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≃</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{n}\simeq\delta_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> we obtain
<math id="S1.p7.m32" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\eta_{ik}\gamma_{i}\simeq(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1})^{-1}\delta_{k-1}\alpha_{k}(\delta_{k}^{-1}\delta_{g})(\gamma_{i+1}\cdots\gamma_{n})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≃</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{ik}\gamma_{i}\simeq(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1})^{-1}\delta_{k-1}\alpha_{k}(\delta_{k}^{-1}\delta_{g})(\gamma_{i+1}\cdots\gamma_{n})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This proves the formula for <math id="S1.p7.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> of Part (b). The calculation of
<math id="S1.p7.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is similar. The closed arc <math id="S1.p7.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is pictured in
the original <math id="S1.p7.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4g</annotation></semantics></math>-polygon on Figure <a href="#S1.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Proof. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> (NW).</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S1.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="/html/math/0509154/assets/irred4.png" id="S1.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" width="517" height="448" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">It is homotopic
to <math id="S1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{ik}\cdot\beta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{ik}\cdot\beta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> is the closed arc
based at <math id="S1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> pictured on Figure <a href="#S1.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Proof. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> (NE). We then consider
<math id="S1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{k}\omega_{ik}\delta_{k}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{k}\omega_{ik}\delta_{k}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Figure <a href="#S1.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Proof. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> (SW)).
The latter is homotopic to <math id="S1.p8.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1})\gamma_{i}(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1})\gamma_{i}(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. We thus
obtain <math id="S1.p8.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\omega_{ik}\simeq(\delta_{k}^{-1}\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1})\gamma_{i}(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{1})^{-1}\delta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≃</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{ik}\simeq(\delta_{k}^{-1}\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1})\gamma_{i}(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{1})^{-1}\delta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. We then
have</span></p>
<table id="S1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\omega_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\omega_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\simeq\delta_{k}^{-1}(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1}\gamma_{i})\gamma_{i}(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1}\gamma_{i})^{-1}\delta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≃</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\simeq\delta_{k}^{-1}(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1}\gamma_{i})\gamma_{i}(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1}\gamma_{i})^{-1}\delta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\simeq[\delta_{k}^{-1}\delta_{g}(\gamma_{i+1}\cdots\gamma_{n})^{-1}]\gamma_{i}[\gamma_{i+1}\cdots\gamma_{n}\delta_{g}^{-1}\delta_{k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≃</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\simeq[\delta_{k}^{-1}\delta_{g}(\gamma_{i+1}\cdots\gamma_{n})^{-1}]\gamma_{i}[\gamma_{i+1}\cdots\gamma_{n}\delta_{g}^{-1}\delta_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="S1.p8.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{n}\simeq\delta_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≃</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{n}\simeq\delta_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>. This proves the
second formula of Part (b).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">(c) The arguments here are very similar to those of
Part (b). One
deforms <math id="S1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}^{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}^{u}</annotation></semantics></math> moving along
the arc <math id="S1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Figure <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 1.5. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). When <math id="S1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}^{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}^{u}</annotation></semantics></math> returns
to <math id="S1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> one obtains closed arcs <math id="S1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{k}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{k}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>
for which <math id="S1.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}^{\prime}\simeq\theta_{ik}\gamma_{i}\theta_{ik}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}^{\prime}\simeq\theta_{ik}\gamma_{i}\theta_{ik}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S1.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{k}^{\prime}=\varepsilon_{ik}\alpha_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{k}^{\prime}=\varepsilon_{ik}\alpha_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S1.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math>
are represented by arcs in the original <math id="S1.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4g</annotation></semantics></math>-polygon pictured on
Figure <a href="#S1.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Proof. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S1.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="/html/math/0509154/assets/irred5.png" id="S1.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" width="502" height="210" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">We calculate <math id="S1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> in the following way. We consider it as a
product of four arcs according to the picture. We deform <math id="S1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math>
in such a way that the first arc becomes a closed simple arc encircling
<math id="S1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{b_{1},\ldots,b_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{b_{1},\ldots,b_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> in clockwise direction, then the second arc goes
from the initial point of <math id="S1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to the end point of
<math id="S1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{k}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{k}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the third arc goes from the initial point of
<math id="S1.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> to the initial point of <math id="S1.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and the fourth arc
equals the first one with the opposite orientation. We have accordingly</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\theta_{ik}\simeq(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i})^{-1}(\delta_{k}\beta_{k})\delta_{k-1}^{-1}(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≃</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{ik}\simeq(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i})^{-1}(\delta_{k}\beta_{k})\delta_{k-1}^{-1}(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Conjugating <math id="S1.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S1.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> we may cancel the last
factor <math id="S1.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S1.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> and replace <math id="S1.p10.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S1.p10.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\gamma_{i+1}\cdots\gamma_{n})\delta_{g}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma_{i+1}\cdots\gamma_{n})\delta_{g}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We thus obtain <math id="S1.p10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}^{\prime}=\nu_{ik}\gamma_{i}\nu_{ik}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}^{\prime}=\nu_{ik}\gamma_{i}\nu_{ik}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> where</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nu_{ik}\ \simeq\ (\gamma_{i+1}\cdots\gamma_{n})(\delta_{k}^{-1}\delta_{g})^{-1}\beta_{k}\delta_{k-1}^{-1}(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≃</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{ik}\ \simeq\ (\gamma_{i+1}\cdots\gamma_{n})(\delta_{k}^{-1}\delta_{g})^{-1}\beta_{k}\delta_{k-1}^{-1}(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, <math id="S1.p10.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\delta_{k-1}\varepsilon_{ik}\delta_{k-1}^{-1}\simeq(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1})\gamma_{i}^{-1}(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{k-1}\varepsilon_{ik}\delta_{k-1}^{-1}\simeq(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1})\gamma_{i}^{-1}(\gamma_{1}\cdots\gamma_{i-1})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This proves the last formula of Part (c).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">In order to obtain the formulas of (d), (e) and (f) from those of (a),
(b) and (c) we notice that if we apply in each case to
<math id="S1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma_{1}^{\prime\prime},\ldots,\gamma_{n}^{\prime\prime};\alpha_{1}^{\prime\prime},\ldots,\beta_{g}^{\prime\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma_{1}^{\prime\prime},\ldots,\gamma_{n}^{\prime\prime};\alpha_{1}^{\prime\prime},\ldots,\beta_{g}^{\prime\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>
the braid moves <math id="S1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j},\rho_{ik},\tau_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j},\rho_{ik},\tau_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively we
obtain
<math id="S1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma_{1},\ldots,\gamma_{n};\alpha_{1},\ldots,\beta_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma_{1},\ldots,\gamma_{n};\alpha_{1},\ldots,\beta_{g})</annotation></semantics></math>. For
example, in order to verify (d) we have <math id="S1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{j}\simeq\gamma_{j+1}^{\prime\prime},\&gt;\gamma_{j+1}\simeq(\gamma_{j+1}^{\prime\prime})^{-1}\gamma_{j}^{\prime\prime}\gamma_{j+1}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≃</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.387em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≃</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{j}\simeq\gamma_{j+1}^{\prime\prime},\&gt;\gamma_{j+1}\simeq(\gamma_{j+1}^{\prime\prime})^{-1}\gamma_{j}^{\prime\prime}\gamma_{j+1}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore
<math id="S1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{j}^{\prime\prime}\simeq\gamma_{j}\gamma_{j+1}\gamma_{j}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{j}^{\prime\prime}\simeq\gamma_{j}\gamma_{j+1}\gamma_{j}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. In
Case (e) applying <math id="S1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S1.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma_{1}^{\prime\prime},\ldots,\beta_{g}^{\prime\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma_{1}^{\prime\prime},\ldots,\beta_{g}^{\prime\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>
we obtain <math id="S1.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{j}\simeq\gamma_{j}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≃</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{j}\simeq\gamma_{j}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S1.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall j\neq i,\&gt;\alpha_{\ell}\simeq\alpha_{\ell}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.387em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>≃</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall j\neq i,\&gt;\alpha_{\ell}\simeq\alpha_{\ell}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S1.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall\ell</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S1.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\ell}\simeq\beta_{\ell}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>≃</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\ell}\simeq\beta_{\ell}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S1.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall\ell\neq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall\ell\neq k</annotation></semantics></math>.
Furthermore <math id="S1.p11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}\simeq\mu_{ik}^{\prime\prime}\gamma_{i}^{\prime\prime}(\mu_{ik}^{\prime\prime})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≃</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}\simeq\mu_{ik}^{\prime\prime}\gamma_{i}^{\prime\prime}(\mu_{ik}^{\prime\prime})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>
where <math id="S1.p11.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{ik}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{ik}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is expressed by
<math id="S1.p11.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{j}^{\prime\prime},\alpha_{\ell}^{\prime\prime},\beta_{\ell}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{j}^{\prime\prime},\alpha_{\ell}^{\prime\prime},\beta_{\ell}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> as in (b). Since neither
<math id="S1.p11.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> nor <math id="S1.p11.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{k}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{k}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> enter in this expression we may replace
<math id="S1.p11.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{j}^{\prime\prime},\alpha_{\ell}^{\prime\prime},\beta_{\ell}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{j}^{\prime\prime},\alpha_{\ell}^{\prime\prime},\beta_{\ell}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> by
<math id="S1.p11.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{j},\alpha_{\ell},\beta_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{j},\alpha_{\ell},\beta_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and we obtain
<math id="S1.p11.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{ik}^{\prime\prime}=\mu_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{ik}^{\prime\prime}=\mu_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus <math id="S1.p11.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}^{\prime\prime}\simeq\mu_{ik}^{-1}\gamma_{i}\mu_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>≃</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}^{\prime\prime}\simeq\mu_{ik}^{-1}\gamma_{i}\mu_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly we have
<math id="S1.p11.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{k}=(\zeta_{ik}\gamma_{i}^{\prime\prime}\zeta_{k}^{-1})\beta_{k}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{k}=(\zeta_{ik}\gamma_{i}^{\prime\prime}\zeta_{k}^{-1})\beta_{k}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> where
<math id="S1.p11.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> is as in (b). Replacing <math id="S1.p11.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> by
<math id="S1.p11.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{ik}^{-1}\gamma_{i}\mu_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{ik}^{-1}\gamma_{i}\mu_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> and canceling we obtain
<math id="S1.p11.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{k}^{\prime\prime}=(\tilde{\zeta}_{ik}^{-1}\gamma_{i}^{-1}\tilde{\zeta}_{ik})\beta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{k}^{\prime\prime}=(\tilde{\zeta}_{ik}^{-1}\gamma_{i}^{-1}\tilde{\zeta}_{ik})\beta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S1.p11.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\zeta}_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\zeta}_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> is as in (e). In a similar
manner one deduces (f) from (c).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Recall from <a href="#S1.Thmthm1" title="1.1. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a> and <a href="#S1.Thmthm2" title="1.2. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a> that given <math id="S1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\in Y^{(n)}-\Delta,\;b_{0}\in Y-D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\in Y^{(n)}-\Delta,\;b_{0}\in Y-D</annotation></semantics></math> and fixing a standard system of
closed arcs
<math id="S1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1},\ldots,\gamma_{n};\alpha_{1},\beta_{1},\ldots,\alpha_{g},\beta_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1},\ldots,\gamma_{n};\alpha_{1},\beta_{1},\ldots,\alpha_{g},\beta_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> there is a bijective correspondence between the
fiber of <math id="S1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y,b_{0})\to(Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y,b_{0})\to(Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> over
<math id="S1.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> and the set of Hurwitz systems
<math id="S1.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g})</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly
there is a bijective correspondence between the fiber of
<math id="S1.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}(b_{0})\to(Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}(b_{0})\to(Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, where
<math id="S1.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}(b_{0})\subset\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}(b_{0})\subset\mathcal{H}_{d}^{(n)}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>, and the set of
equivalence classes of Hurwitz systems
<math id="S1.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g}]</annotation></semantics></math>. In the next
theorem we calculate the monodromy action of
<math id="S1.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}((Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta,D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}((Y-b_{0})^{(n)}-\Delta,D)</annotation></semantics></math> on these fibers. According to
Proposition <a href="#S1.Thmthm6" title="Proposition 1.6 (Birman). ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.6</span></a> it suffices to determine the braid moves
which correspond to the generators <math id="S1.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j},\rho_{ik},\tau_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j},\rho_{ik},\tau_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math>. We
denote the corresponding braid moves of the first type (cf.
Definition <a href="#Thmdfn2" title="Definition 2. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) by <math id="S1.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j}^{\prime},\rho_{ik}^{\prime},\tau_{ik}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j}^{\prime},\rho_{ik}^{\prime},\tau_{ik}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and we
denote the corresponding braid moves of the second type (inverse to those of
the
first type) by <math id="S1.p12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j}^{\prime\prime},\rho_{ik}^{\prime\prime},\tau_{ik}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j}^{\prime\prime},\rho_{ik}^{\prime\prime},\tau_{ik}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmthm8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1.8</span></span><span id="S1.Thmthm8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmthm8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S1.Thmthm8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g})</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S1.Thmthm8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{g+k}=\mu_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{g+k}=\mu_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, be a Hurwitz system. Let
<math id="S1.Thmthm8.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u_{k}=[\lambda_{1},\mu_{1}]\cdots[\lambda_{k},\mu_{k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k}=[\lambda_{1},\mu_{1}]\cdots[\lambda_{k},\mu_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math> for
<math id="S1.Thmthm8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,\ldots,g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,\ldots,g</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="S1.Thmthm8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{0}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{0}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. The following formulas hold for the
braid moves
<math id="S1.Thmthm8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g})\mapsto(t^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,t^{\prime}_{n};\lambda^{\prime}_{1},\mu^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,\lambda^{\prime}_{g},\mu^{\prime}_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g})\mapsto(t^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,t^{\prime}_{n};\lambda^{\prime}_{1},\mu^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,\lambda^{\prime}_{g},\mu^{\prime}_{g})</annotation></semantics></math> of the
first type.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm8.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm8.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">a. For <math id="S1.Thmthm8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S1.Thmthm8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq j\leq n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq j\leq n-1</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle t^{\prime}_{i}=t_{i}\quad\text{for $\forall i\neq j,\,j+1$},\quad\lambda^{\prime}_{\ell}=\lambda_{\ell},\quad\mu^{\prime}_{\ell}=\mu_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell$}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle t^{\prime}_{i}=t_{i}\quad\text{for $\forall i\neq j,\,j+1$},\quad\lambda^{\prime}_{\ell}=\lambda_{\ell},\quad\mu^{\prime}_{\ell}=\mu_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(t_{j},t_{j+1})\ \mapsto\ (t^{\prime}_{j},t^{\prime}_{j+1})\ =\ (t_{j}t_{j+1}t_{j}^{-1}\,,\,t_{j})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em" stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(t_{j},t_{j+1})\ \mapsto\ (t^{\prime}_{j},t^{\prime}_{j+1})\ =\ (t_{j}t_{j+1}t_{j}^{-1}\,,\,t_{j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm8.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm8.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">b. For <math id="S1.Thmthm8.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{ik}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{ik}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S1.Thmthm8.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n,\;1\leq k\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n,\;1\leq k\leq g</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle t^{\prime}_{j}=t_{j}\quad\text{for $\forall j\neq i$},\quad\lambda^{\prime}_{\ell}=\lambda_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell$},\quad\mu^{\prime}_{\ell}=\mu_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell\neq k$}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle t^{\prime}_{j}=t_{j}\quad\text{for $\forall j\neq i$},\quad\lambda^{\prime}_{\ell}=\lambda_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell$},\quad\mu^{\prime}_{\ell}=\mu_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell\neq k$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(t_{i},\mu_{k})\ \mapsto\ (t^{\prime}_{i},\mu^{\prime}_{k})\ =\ (a_{1}^{-1}t_{i}a_{1},(b_{1}^{-1}t_{i}^{-1}b_{1})\mu_{k})\quad\text{where}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em" stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(t_{i},\mu_{k})\ \mapsto\ (t^{\prime}_{i},\mu^{\prime}_{k})\ =\ (a_{1}^{-1}t_{i}a_{1},(b_{1}^{-1}t_{i}^{-1}b_{1})\mu_{k})\quad\text{where}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle a_{1}=(t_{1}\cdots t_{i-1})^{-1}u_{k-1}\lambda_{k}(u_{k}^{-1}u_{g})(t_{i+1}\cdots t_{n})^{-1},\quad b_{1}=(t_{1}\cdots t_{i-1})^{-1}u_{k-1}\lambda_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a_{1}=(t_{1}\cdots t_{i-1})^{-1}u_{k-1}\lambda_{k}(u_{k}^{-1}u_{g})(t_{i+1}\cdots t_{n})^{-1},\quad b_{1}=(t_{1}\cdots t_{i-1})^{-1}u_{k-1}\lambda_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm8.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm8.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm8.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">c. For <math id="S1.Thmthm8.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{ik}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{ik}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S1.Thmthm8.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n,\;1\leq k\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n,\;1\leq k\leq g</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle t^{\prime}_{j}=t_{j}\quad\text{for $\forall j\neq i$},\quad\lambda^{\prime}_{\ell}=\lambda_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell\neq k$},\quad\mu^{\prime}_{\ell}=\mu_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell$}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle t^{\prime}_{j}=t_{j}\quad\text{for $\forall j\neq i$},\quad\lambda^{\prime}_{\ell}=\lambda_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell\neq k$},\quad\mu^{\prime}_{\ell}=\mu_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(t_{i},\lambda_{k})\ \mapsto\ (t^{\prime}_{i},\lambda^{\prime}_{k})\ =\ (c_{1}^{-1}t_{i}c_{1},(d_{1}^{-1}t_{i}d_{1})\lambda_{k})\quad\text{where}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em" stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(t_{i},\lambda_{k})\ \mapsto\ (t^{\prime}_{i},\lambda^{\prime}_{k})\ =\ (c_{1}^{-1}t_{i}c_{1},(d_{1}^{-1}t_{i}d_{1})\lambda_{k})\quad\text{where}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle c_{1}=t_{i+1}\cdots t_{n}(u_{k}^{-1}u_{g})^{-1}\mu_{k}(u_{k-1})^{-1}t_{1}\cdots t_{i-1},\quad d_{1}=t_{i+1}\cdots t_{n}(u_{k}^{-1}u_{g})^{-1}\mu_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{1}=t_{i+1}\cdots t_{n}(u_{k}^{-1}u_{g})^{-1}\mu_{k}(u_{k-1})^{-1}t_{1}\cdots t_{i-1},\quad d_{1}=t_{i+1}\cdots t_{n}(u_{k}^{-1}u_{g})^{-1}\mu_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.Thmthm8.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm8.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The following formulas hold for the
braid moves
<math id="S1.Thmthm8.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g})\mapsto\linebreak(t^{\prime\prime}_{1},\ldots,t^{\prime\prime}_{n};\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{1},\mu^{\prime\prime}_{1},\ldots,\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{g},\mu^{\prime\prime}_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{1},\ldots,t_{n};\lambda_{1},\mu_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{g},\mu_{g})\mapsto\linebreak(t^{\prime\prime}_{1},\ldots,t^{\prime\prime}_{n};\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{1},\mu^{\prime\prime}_{1},\ldots,\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{g},\mu^{\prime\prime}_{g})</annotation></semantics></math> of the
second type.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm8.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm8.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm8.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">d. For <math id="S1.Thmthm8.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S1.Thmthm8.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq j\leq n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq j\leq n-1</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle t^{\prime\prime}_{i}=t_{i}\quad\text{for $\forall i\neq j,\,j+1$},\quad\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{\ell}=\lambda_{\ell},\quad\mu^{\prime\prime}_{\ell}=\mu_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell$}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle t^{\prime\prime}_{i}=t_{i}\quad\text{for $\forall i\neq j,\,j+1$},\quad\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{\ell}=\lambda_{\ell},\quad\mu^{\prime\prime}_{\ell}=\mu_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(t_{j},t_{j+1})\ \mapsto\ (t^{\prime\prime}_{j},t^{\prime\prime}_{j+1})\ =\ (t_{j+1}\,,\,t_{j+1}^{-1}t_{j}t_{j+1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em" stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(t_{j},t_{j+1})\ \mapsto\ (t^{\prime\prime}_{j},t^{\prime\prime}_{j+1})\ =\ (t_{j+1}\,,\,t_{j+1}^{-1}t_{j}t_{j+1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm8.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm8.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm8.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e. For <math id="S1.Thmthm8.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{ik}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{ik}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S1.Thmthm8.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n,\;1\leq k\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n,\;1\leq k\leq g</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle t^{\prime\prime}_{j}=t_{j}\quad\text{for $\forall j\neq i$},\quad\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{\ell}=\lambda_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell$},\quad\mu^{\prime\prime}_{\ell}=\mu_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell\neq k$}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle t^{\prime\prime}_{j}=t_{j}\quad\text{for $\forall j\neq i$},\quad\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{\ell}=\lambda_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell$},\quad\mu^{\prime\prime}_{\ell}=\mu_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell\neq k$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(t_{i},\mu_{k})\ \mapsto\ (t^{\prime\prime}_{i},\mu^{\prime\prime}_{k})\ =\ (a_{2}^{-1}t_{i}a_{2},(b_{2}^{-1}t_{i}b_{2})\mu_{k})\quad\text{where}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em" stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(t_{i},\mu_{k})\ \mapsto\ (t^{\prime\prime}_{i},\mu^{\prime\prime}_{k})\ =\ (a_{2}^{-1}t_{i}a_{2},(b_{2}^{-1}t_{i}b_{2})\mu_{k})\quad\text{where}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle a_{2}=t_{i+1}\cdots t_{n}(u_{k}^{-1}u_{g})^{-1}\lambda_{k}^{-1}(u_{k-1})^{-1}t_{1}\cdots t_{i-1},\quad b_{2}=t_{i+1}\cdots t_{n}(u_{k}^{-1}u_{g})^{-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a_{2}=t_{i+1}\cdots t_{n}(u_{k}^{-1}u_{g})^{-1}\lambda_{k}^{-1}(u_{k-1})^{-1}t_{1}\cdots t_{i-1},\quad b_{2}=t_{i+1}\cdots t_{n}(u_{k}^{-1}u_{g})^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm8.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm8.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm8.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">f. For <math id="S1.Thmthm8.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{ik}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{ik}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S1.Thmthm8.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n,\;1\leq k\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n,\;1\leq k\leq g</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle t^{\prime\prime}_{j}=t_{j}\quad\text{for $\forall j\neq i$},\quad\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{\ell}=\lambda_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell\neq k$},\quad\mu^{\prime\prime}_{\ell}=\mu_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell$}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle t^{\prime\prime}_{j}=t_{j}\quad\text{for $\forall j\neq i$},\quad\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{\ell}=\lambda_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell\neq k$},\quad\mu^{\prime\prime}_{\ell}=\mu_{\ell}\quad\text{for $\forall\ell$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(t_{i},\lambda_{k})\ \mapsto\ (t^{\prime\prime}_{i},\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{k})\ =\ (c_{2}^{-1}t_{i}c_{2},(d_{2}^{-1}t_{i}^{-1}d_{2})\lambda_{k})\quad\text{where}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em" stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(t_{i},\lambda_{k})\ \mapsto\ (t^{\prime\prime}_{i},\lambda^{\prime\prime}_{k})\ =\ (c_{2}^{-1}t_{i}c_{2},(d_{2}^{-1}t_{i}^{-1}d_{2})\lambda_{k})\quad\text{where}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle c_{2}=(t_{1}\cdots t_{i-1})^{-1}u_{k-1}\mu_{k}^{-1}(u_{k}^{-1}u_{g})(t_{i+1}\cdots t_{n})^{-1},\quad d_{2}=(t_{1}\cdots t_{i-1})^{-1}u_{k-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{2}=(t_{1}\cdots t_{i-1})^{-1}u_{k-1}\mu_{k}^{-1}(u_{k}^{-1}u_{g})(t_{i+1}\cdots t_{n})^{-1},\quad d_{2}=(t_{1}\cdots t_{i-1})^{-1}u_{k-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Formulas (d), (e) and (f) are obtained from formulas (a),
(b) and (c) of Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm7" title="Theorem 1.7. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.7</span></a> respectively applying the homomorphism
<math id="S1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m:\pi_{1}(Y-D,b_{0})\to S_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m:\pi_{1}(Y-D,b_{0})\to S_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and equalities Eq.(<a href="#S1.E4" title="In 1.3. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) and
Eq.(<a href="#S1.E5" title="In 1.3. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>). By Lemma <a href="#S1.Thmthm4" title="Lemma 1.4. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.4</span></a> the braid moves of the first
type are inverse to the braid moves of the second type. We may thus
obtain formulas (a), (b) and (c) from formulas (d), (e)
and (f) of Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm7" title="Theorem 1.7. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.7</span></a> respectively applying the homomorphism <math id="S1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmthm9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 1.9</span></span><span id="S1.Thmthm9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmthm9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Using the notation of Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm8" title="Theorem 1.8. ‣ 1 Braid moves ‣ Irreducibility of Hurwitz spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.8</span></a> the following formulas hold.</span></p>
<ol id="S1.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">i.</span> 
<div id="S1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For </span><math id="S1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{ik}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{ik}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">  :</span></p>
<table id="S1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rho^{\prime}_{nk}:t_{n}\mapsto t^{\prime}_{n}=a_{1}^{-1}t_{n}a_{1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rho^{\prime}_{nk}:t_{n}\mapsto t^{\prime}_{n}=a_{1}^{-1}t_{n}a_{1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S1.Ex40.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_italic">where
<math id="S1.Ex40.m2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}=(u_{k}^{-1}u_{g})^{-1}[\mu_{k},\lambda_{k}]\lambda_{k}(u_{k}^{-1}u_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}=(u_{k}^{-1}u_{g})^{-1}[\mu_{k},\lambda_{k}]\lambda_{k}(u_{k}^{-1}u_{g})</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rho_{1k}^{\prime}:\mu_{k}\mapsto\mu_{k}^{\prime}=(b_{1}^{-1}t_{1}^{-1}b_{1})\mu_{k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rho_{1k}^{\prime}:\mu_{k}\mapsto\mu_{k}^{\prime}=(b_{1}^{-1}t_{1}^{-1}b_{1})\mu_{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S1.Ex41.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_italic">where
<math id="S1.Ex41.m2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{1}=u_{k-1}\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{1}=u_{k-1}\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rho_{nk}^{\prime}:\mu_{k}\mapsto\mu^{\prime}_{k}=(b_{1}^{-1}t_{n}^{-1}b_{1})\mu_{k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rho_{nk}^{\prime}:\mu_{k}\mapsto\mu^{\prime}_{k}=(b_{1}^{-1}t_{n}^{-1}b_{1})\mu_{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{where $b_{1}=(u_{k}^{-1}u_{g})^{-1}[\mu_{k},\lambda_{k}]\lambda_{k}$}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where </mtext><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{where $b_{1}=(u_{k}^{-1}u_{g})^{-1}[\mu_{k},\lambda_{k}]\lambda_{k}$}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">ii.</span> 
<div id="S1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For </span><math id="S1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{\prime}_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{\prime}_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">  :</span></p>
